f=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-15\" transform=\"translate(162.609375 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-16\" transform=\"translate(199.3125 0)\"/></g></g></g><g id=\"patch_3\"><path d=\"M 51.025455 133.76 L 190.807273 133.76 L 190.807273 17.6 L 51.025455 17.6 z\n\" clip-path=\"url(#p6b7292ee9d)\" style=\"fill: #0a8f9c\"/></g><g id=\"patch_4\"><path d=\"M 225.752727 133.76 L 365.534545 133.76 L 365.534545 78.445714 L 225.752727 78.445714 z\n\" clip-path=\"url(#p6b7292ee9d)\" style=\"fill: #c2410c\"/></g><g id=\"patch_5\"><path d=\"M 35.3 133.76 L 35.3 11.792 \" style=\"fill: none; stroke: #c9d1dc; stroke-width: 0.8; stroke-linejoin: miter; stroke-linecap: square\"/></g><g id=\"patch_6\"><path d=\"M 35.3 133.76 L 381.26 133.76 \" style=\"fill: none; stroke: #c9d1dc; stroke-width: 0.8; stroke-linejoin: miter; stroke-linecap: square\"/></g><g id=\"text_9\"><g style=\"fill: #2d3748\" transform=\"translate(115.028239 15.4) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-5a\" d=\"M 870 -77 Q 672 -77 576 28 Q 480 134 480 294 L 480 378 Q 480 544 576 646 Q 672 749 870 749 Q 1075 749 1168 646 Q 1261 544 1261 378 L 1261 294 Q 1261 134 1168 28 Q 1075 -77 870 -77 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-42\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-5a\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3e\" transform=\"translate(87.203125 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_10\"><g style=\"fill: #2d3748\" transform=\"translate(289.755511 76.245714) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3e\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-5a\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-38\" transform=\"translate(87.203125 0)\"/></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"p6b7292ee9d\"><rect x=\"35.3\" y=\"11.792\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"121.968\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · Payback in years","note":null},"answer":"<p>Volume rises to 1,478 tonnes. Saving: 1,478k × $0.47 − $250k = <b>$445k</b>. Payback: <b>4.0 years</b>, within target.</p> <p><b>So-what:</b> the decision depends on the expansion. Build only if the new hotels are committed, and size the plant for them. This assumes the $1.8M plant can handle the larger volume and the new hotels are open from the start: if the plant ran on today's volume for two years first, payback would be about 5.1 years, so time the build to the openings.</p>"},{"q":"What else would you check before deciding?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<ul><li><b>Quality and speed:</b> does the outside laundry cause complaints or stock-outs?</li><li><b>Risk:</b> one plant serving all hotels needs a backup contract</li> <li><b>Contract:</b> could Heatherfield negotiate a lower outside price with its larger volume, which may beat building?</li><li><b>Site and staff:</b> land, permits, hiring</li></ul>"}],"reco":"Don't build the laundry on today's six hotels: it saves about $213k a year, a payback of 8.4 years against a five-year target. If the three new hotels are committed, the saving rises to about $445k and payback falls to 4.0 years, so build when they open (two years at today's volume first would push payback to about 5.1 years), sized for 1,350 rooms. Meanwhile, use the coming volume to negotiate a lower price with the outside laundry. Risk: a single plant is a single point of failure, so keep a backup contract.","great":["Computes volume from rooms and occupancy","Separates variable from fixed costs","Works out the volume needed to hit the target","Ties the answer to the expansion plan"],"id":51,"slug":"heatherfield-hotels"}